  "summary": "CGI::Cookie versions before 5.00 for Perl allow cookie attribute injection via unvalidated path, domain and expires…",
  "details": "CGI::Cookie versions before 5.00 for Perl allow cookie attribute injection via unvalidated path, domain and expires values.\n\nThe path, domain and expires values are written into the Set-Cookie header without checking for semicolons or control characters.\n\nAn application that sets them from request data can be made to add other cookie attributes, such as Domain or SameSite.",
